951d91fc00be" :question/math-academy-id "q-88460" :question/problem "What is the product of solutions of the equation $2{x}^{2}\\cdot {6}^{x+3}-9x\\cdot {6}^{x+3}+4\\cdot {6}^{x+3}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}\\cdot {6}^{x+3}-9x\\cdot {6}^{x+3}+4\\cdot {6}^{x+3} & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}-9x+4){6}^{x+3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}-9x+4=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{6}^{x+3}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $2{x}^{2}-9x+4=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(2x-1)(x-4)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=\\frac{1}{2},4.$\n\n- The equation ${6}^{x+3}=0$ has no solutions because ${6}^{x+3}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=\\frac{1}{2},4,$ and their product is $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-88460/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3758cf02-ba4b-539a-bc61-8c2030ff6f6f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88460"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-237946/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "09d7897f-e3b2-57b2-b7b1-01f92a0ec301" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-237946/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "f1ab6678-a097-55ca-93a7-3ef7b79398f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-237946/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "24f5bd3d-59cf-5b72-8150-e5c8201e3656" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-237946/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :