"q-237946/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3758cf02-ba4b-539a-bc61-8c2030ff6f6f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-237946"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-264778/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "eda9e078-1943-5ebd-935c-afdc99ead1b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264778/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e926dec-382f-56be-b32f-b0ebe932a898" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264778/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-264778/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264778/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "cf560934-9e52-58f3-a07f-85136b73967e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264778/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec25c2f2-d84e-512e-b94a-6d9fdc97a5b6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264778/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-264778/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264778" :question/id #uuid "7122b6e0-4bf0-565b-88a8-baed162e5764" :question/math-academy-id "q-264778" :question/problem "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation $2{x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{x+3}-7x\\cdot {2}^{x+3}+3\\cdot {2}^{x+3}=0$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{x+3}-7x\\cdot {2}^{x+3}+3\\cdot {2}^{x+3} & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}-7x+3){2}^{x+3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}-7x+3=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{2}^{x+3}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $2{x}^{2}-7x+3=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(2x-1)(x-3)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=\\frac{1}{2},3.$\n\n- The equation ${2}^{x+3}=0$ has no solutions because ${2}^{x+3}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{and}\\,x=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-264778/field-1" "q-264778/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3758cf02-ba4b-539a-bc61-8c2030ff6f6f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-264778"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-264786/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "0a47b2ec-48db-586c-83c7-6986d749de3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264786/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "3e596de6-42b8-5a22-a832-311c3c37b97a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264786/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b4874eb-da20-5fbe-98e8-a7d3cc21e86a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264786/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-264786/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-264786/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264786/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "934c528d-b0cd-55f4-ac56-4393ebb6b5a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264786/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c64c6ea-e067-59f6-8d72-bd26b1e98cdc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264786/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-264786/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264786" :question/id #uuid "a3bb3ced-7db7-5b87-94c1-62537aeec042" :question/math-academy-id "q-264786" :question/problem "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation $2{x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{2x-5}=50\\cdot {3}^{2x-5}$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{2x-5} & =50\\cdot {3}^{2x-5} \\\\ 2{x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{2x-5}-50\\cdot {3}^{2x-5} & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}-50)\\cdot {3}^{2x-5} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}-50=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{3}^{2x-5}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $2{x}^{2}-50=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}^{2}-25) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+5)(x-5) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-5,5.$\n\n- The equation $2=0$ is not a possible solution because it's a false statement.\n\n- The equation ${3}^{2x-5}=0$ has no solutions because ${3}^{2x-5}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=-5\\,\\text{and}\\,x=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-264786/field-1" "q-264786/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aaf12cf-8596-5960-bc68-5ca3eb5fab0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-264786"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-264793/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "df3889dc-037c-57b4-b1e8-6f1ded27af82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264793/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee2c1396-2e55-5c8d-8ebf-daab6e87b537" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264793/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer-field/choices ["q-264793/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264793/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "e94f7cbc-7ffa-58a9-94e7-e5b531bc989c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264793/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8cc6704d-aa5b-5127-87b8-aea648b10e80" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264793/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-264793/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264793" :question/id #uuid "b6c4f0ee-1545-58ee-a3be-5f0c616e95a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-264793" :question/problem "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation $4{x}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{2x}+6\\cdot {e}^{2x}=25x\\cdot {e}^{2x}$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{2x}+6\\cdot {e}^{2x} & =25x\\cdot {e}^{2x} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{2x}-25x\\cdot {e}^{2x}+6\\cdot {e}^{2x} & =0 \\\\ (4{x}^{2}-25x+6)\\cdot {e}^{2x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-25x+6=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{e}^{2x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $4{x}^{2}-25x+6=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(4x-1)(x-6)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=\\frac{1}{4},x=6.$\n\n- The equation ${e}^{2x}=0$ has no solutions because ${e}^{2x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{and}\\,x=6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-264793/field-1" "q-264793/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aaf12cf-8596-5960-bc68-5ca3eb5fab0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-264793"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
